# swift-cross-ui v0.8.0 GtkBackend Windows input fix — ROUND 7 (CUESYNC-9)
#
# Pinned to tag v0.8.0, commit a6d206370812e3b9edba259d167e848892c5013d. Applied by
# scripts/patch-swift-cross-ui.sh (box + dev) and .github/workflows/swift-windows.yml
# (CI) to the resolved checkout at .build/checkouts/swift-cross-ui, AFTER the
# gtk-interactivity patch and BEFORE the gsk-renderer patch. The script now resets
# the checkout to pristine before applying, so this file fully SUPERSEDES the
# round-1/round-2 content (priority + floor + pre-drain around a still-running
# `RunLoop.main` pump) — do not stack them.
#
# Root cause (specs/CUESYNC-9-findings.md §3, CONFIRMED by the round-6 startup log:
# banner present, zero Pango/fontconfig lines, zero GSK/GL lines, window real and
# full-size, input dead): GtkBackend's mainRunLoopTicklingLoop (upstream PR #141,
# added so @MainActor / DispatchQueue.main work off-Apple) ticks Foundation's
# `RunLoop.main` on Windows. swift-corelibs-foundation binds `RunLoop.main` to this
# thread's Win32 message queue (`_CFRunLoopSetWindowsMessageQueueMask(_, QS_ALLINPUT,
# ...)`), and CoreFoundation's run-loop pass PeekMessage/DispatchMessage-drains that
# queue — the SAME queue GDK's win32 backend needs for mouse/keyboard/close input.
# Two uncoordinated consumers, one queue: Foundation eats the input, GTK renders a
# window that never feels a click. Rounds 1-2 lowered the tickler's priority and
# floored its reschedule — the theft got rarer, not impossible, and the probe stayed
# click-dead (also: rounds 1-5 never actually reached the box build — see
# scripts/patch-swift-cross-ui.sh and the ci-local/click-probe prepare step).
#
# Fix, structural: on Windows, NEVER pump `RunLoop.main`. Service what PR #141
# actually needs — libdispatch's main queue (which is what @MainActor jobs and
# DispatchQueue.main enqueue to on non-Darwin) — by calling libdispatch's own
# CF-integration hook `_dispatch_main_queue_callback_4CF` directly from the GLib
# tickler. Foundation then never touches the Win32 queue at all; GDK is its sole
# owner. The tickler stays at G_PRIORITY_DEFAULT_IDLE with an 8 ms floor so GDK
# input/redraw always preempts it. Linux/macOS: byte-identical to upstream.
#
# Known, accepted cost (verified absent from swift-cross-ui and Cue Sync by grep):
# Foundation `Timer`/`RunLoop.main.perform` scheduled work will not fire on Windows.
#
# Idempotency: the apply script resets the checkout pristine first; CI guards with
# `git apply --reverse --check` before applying.
diff --git a/Sources/GtkBackend/GtkBackend.swift b/Sources/GtkBackend/GtkBackend.swift
